        <body>
            <div xml:id="d577">

                <pb facs="0705" n="603" sameAs="frus:frus1908/pg603"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">File No. 8183/165–169.</note>
                <head><hi rendition="#italic">Chargé Sands to the Secretary of State.</hi></head>
                <opener><dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >American Embassy</hi>,<lb/><hi rendition="#italic"
                            >Mexico</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian" when="1908-09-18"
                                ><hi rendition="#italic">September 18, 1908</hi></date>.</dateline>
                    <seg rendition="#float-left">No. 1244.]</seg></opener>
                <p><hi rendition="#small-caps">Sir</hi>: For the information of the department, I
                    inclose herewith clippings from the Mexican Herald of yesterday and to-day, on
                    the subject of the opening by President Diaz of the first period of sessions of
                    the Twenty-fourth Congress, on the evening of the 16th instant, and the
                    President’s message delivered on that occasion.</p>
                <p>I have, etc.,</p>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">W. F. Sands.</hi></signed></closer>



                <xi:include href="d577-a1.xml" xpointer="d577-a1"/>
            </div>
